<title>JAPAN: Japan June beef imports rise 29.0 pct yr/yr--MOF.</title>
<headline>Japan June beef imports rise 29.0 pct yr/yr--MOF.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's beef imports in June totalled 64,290 tonnes, up 29.0 percent from the same month a year earlier, Finance Ministry data released on Tuesday showed.</p>
<p>The details were as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		    June 97	May 97    June 96</p>
<p> Total	    64,290	 45,877     49,826</p>
<p> Refrigerated   27,396	 27,661     23,565</p>
<p> Frozen	   36,894	 18,216     26,261</p>
<p>Major suppliers of refrigerated beef (in tonnes):</p>
<p>  Australia     16,454	 14,764     13,709</p>
<p>  U.S.	    10,014	 11,928	8,790</p>
<p>Major suppliers of frozen beef (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		    June 97	 May 97    June 96</p>
<p>  U.S.	    19,274	  9,042     13,728</p>
<p>  Australia     14,334	  7,410	9,505</p>
<p>Cumulative imports of refrigerated beef in the first six months of 1997 were 157,338 tonnes against 166,491 tonnes a year earlier.</p>
<p>Frozen beef imports in the January-June period of this year were 145,631 tonnes against 175,364 tonnes in the year-ago period.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk (+81-3-3432-7391)</p>
</text>
